<v Yang Yi>Yes, yes, of course. I say, OK, self-test is negative today. There's no need for it. And they say, oh, you guys have to go.
<v Yang Yi>是的，是的，当然。我说，好的，自我测试今天呈阴性。不需要它了。他们说，噢，你们必须去。

00:36:18.640 --> 00:36:21.450
<v Ira Glass>What if you don't go?
<v Ira Glass>如果你不去会怎样？

00:36:21.450 --> 00:36:24.390
<v Yang Yi>Who knows? I have no idea.
<v Yang Yi>谁知道呢？我一点头绪都没有。

00:36:24.390 --> 00:36:25.890
<v Ira Glass>Really?
<v Ira Glass>真的吗？

00:36:25.890 --> 00:36:27.360
<v Yang Yi>Yeah.
<v Yang Yi>是的。

00:36:27.360 --> 00:36:51.430
<v Ira Glass>They decide that it's smart to go because now they have this bureaucratic thing that they actually need to fix. China has these QR codes. Everybody has one on their phone. Red if you have COVID, green if you don't have COVID. Now theirs were red, meaning they wouldn't be able to go into any building or store or office or just anywhere when lockdown ended. That's the thing they thought the quarantine center could cure for them.
<v Ira Glass>他们认为去是明智的，因为现在他们有一件官僚事务确实需要解决。中国有这些二维码。每个人的手机上都有一个。如果你有新冠是红色的，如果你没有新冠是绿色的。现在他们的是红色的，这意味着当封锁结束时，他们将无法进入任何建筑物、商店、办公室或任何地方。这就是他们认为隔离中心可以为他们治愈的事情。

00:36:51.430 --> 00:36:59.550
<v Yang Yi>And at that point, my thought is we want a healthy social identity back, not a healthy body.
<v Yang Yi>在那一刻，我的想法是我们想要回一个健康的社会身份，而不是一个健康的身体。

00:36:59.550 --> 00:37:02.130
<v Yang Yi>[LAUGHTER]
<v Yang Yi>[笑声]

00:37:02.130 --> 00:37:07.590
<v Ira Glass>Exactly. Even if your bodies don't have COVID, your QR code has COVID, and they can take care of that.
<v Ira Glass>确实。即使你们的身体没有新冠，你们的二维码有新冠，他们可以处理那个。

00:37:07.590 --> 00:37:13.880
<v Yang Yi>Yes.
<v Yang Yi>是的。

00:37:13.880 --> 00:37:20.060
<v Ira Glass>So, after a week, you finally go to the quarantine center. What's it like?
<v Ira Glass>所以，在一周后，你们终于去了隔离中心。那是什么样的？

00:37:20.060 --> 00:37:24.950
<v Yang Yi>Actually, it is a high school gymnasium.
<v Yang Yi>实际上，它是一个高中体育馆。

00:37:24.950 --> 00:37:28.690
<v Yang Yi>[DOCTORS SPEAKING IN CHINESE]
<v Yang Yi>[医生讲中文]

00:37:28.690 --> 00:37:44.490
<v Yang Yi>And this is sound I recorded for my own podcast. And this quarantine center is for people with very mild symptoms or no symptoms at all. Most don't even need a doctor. So they just come here and rest and wait to get better.
<v Yang Yi>这是我为自己的播客录下的声音。这个隔离中心是给那些症状非常轻微甚至根本没有症状的人准备的。大多数人甚至不需要医生。所以他们只是来到这里休息并等待康复。

00:37:44.490 --> 00:37:50.060
<v Yang Yi>[DOCTORS SPEAKING IN CHINESE]
<v Yang Yi>[医生讲中文]

00:37:50.060 --> 00:38:00.060
<v Yang Yi>These are doctors telling us all where to go. You go to the first floor. You are first, you are second, you are third. OK, move forward.
<v Yang Yi>这些是医生告诉我们大家去哪里。你们去一楼。你是第一批，你是第二批，你是第三批。好的，向前走。

00:38:00.060 --> 00:38:00.980
<v Ira Glass>Then what happens?
<v Ira Glass>然后发生了什么？

00:38:00.980 --> 00:38:13.940
<v Yang Yi>My boyfriend and I go inside. They issued us toiletries, a washbasin, toothpaste, toothbrush, towel, a cup, and two packet of tissues.
<v Yang Yi>我和我男朋友进去了。他们发给我们洗漱用品，一个洗脸盆，牙膏，牙刷，毛巾，一个杯子和两包纸巾。

00:38:13.940 --> 00:38:15.320
<v Ira Glass>Two packets of tissues.
<v Ira Glass>两包纸巾。

00:38:15.320 --> 00:38:19.700
<v Yang Yi>And a sleeping bag. And we wait for check-in.
<v Yang Yi>还有一个睡袋。然后我们等待办理入住。

00:38:19.700 --> 00:38:21.950
<v Ira Glass>It's like you guys are joining the army or something.
<v Ira Glass>听起来你们就像是去参军什么的。

00:38:21.950 --> 00:38:24.180
<v Yang Yi>[LAUGHS]
<v Yang Yi>[笑]

00:38:24.180 --> 00:38:29.210
<v Yang Yi>[SPEAKING CHINESE]
<v Yang Yi>[讲中文]

00:38:29.210 --> 00:38:56.960
<v Ira Glass>Some people are sent to stay on the basketball court on the third floor. He and Johnny were pointed to the first floor, where they learned they'd be living in the swimming pool. There's no water in it. Instead, there were rows of cots, men in the deep end, women and children in the shallow end. Elderly people with mobility problems were on the edges of the pool. Because it was just a high school pool, there's only a tiny bathroom with one toilet in it for the men and another bathroom with one toilet for the women.
<v Ira Glass>有些人被派去睡在三楼的篮球场上。他和强尼被指引到一楼，在那里他们得知将住在游泳池里。里面没有水。取而代之的是一排排帆布床，男的在深水区，妇女和儿童在浅水区。有行动障碍的老人在池边。因为这只是一个高中游泳池，男士那边只有一个带一个厕所的小浴室，女士那边有另一个带一个厕所的浴室。

00:38:56.960 --> 00:39:06.660
<v Yang Yi>But there are close to 200 people here now. So it's crazy. And there is no hot water in the shower.
<v Yang Yi>但现在这里有近200人。所以这太疯狂了。而且淋浴间里没有热水。

00:39:06.660 --> 00:39:15.650
<v Ira Glass>Yi and Johnny figured they'd be there for four or five days. The rumor was, you needed two negative PCR tests to get out. And they give the tests every other day.
<v Ira Glass>杨和强尼估计他们会在那里待上四五天。传言说，你需要两次阴性PCR测试才能出去。他们每隔一天进行测试。

00:39:15.650 --> 00:39:25.580
<v Yang Yi>It was late at night when we arrived. So we went straight to bed. So in a quarantine center, the lights do not turn off all night long.
<v Yang Yi>我们到达时已经是深夜了。所以我们直接上床睡觉了。所以在一个隔离中心，灯光整夜都不会熄灭。

00:39:25.580 --> 00:39:27.050
<v Ira Glass>The lights don't turn off?
<v Ira Glass>灯不会关吗？

00:39:27.050 --> 00:39:34.970
<v Yang Yi>And people around you watch TikTok all night long without headphones on.
<v Yang Yi>而且周围的人整夜不戴耳机看抖音。

00:39:34.970 --> 00:39:38.720
<v Yang Yi>[SPEAKING CHINESE]
<v Yang Yi>[讲中文]

00:39:38.720 --> 00:39:40.160
<v Ira Glass>OK, so that's you.
<v Ira Glass>好吧，那是在你身上。

00:39:40.160 --> 00:39:51.960
<v Yang Yi>Saying it is now 10:40 PM on April the 17th. I'm laying on the cot. And you can hear what it sounds like around me.
<v Yang Yi>说现在是4月17日晚上10:40。我躺在床上。你可以听到我周围的声音。

00:39:51.960 --> 00:39:57.110
<v Yang Yi>[NOISE]
<v Yang Yi>[噪音]

